{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for draft2, sole artifact notes/2026-10-16-repo-in-ai-mvp-plan.md at88fc23a931894925cad8d445c5707b267b461a33/treefab68488406af8e398a0b9710a2f32da9b9bfeeb. This reviews the new scope on its own terms and reconciles prior review90cde2a1. No objection to the settled choice of an existing hosted room reached through local MCP, a trusted example package, or question text with requested human approvals.\n\nThe new manual data path is supported by Source: activated definitions plus set-actions (docs/run-your-app.md:103-147), directory open-issue's active-definition guard and digest-pinned create (directory.ts:126-145,727-750). These support a CONDITIONAL no-new-host-code path; S0 must still establish the deployed service's routes/forms and actual chosen room/destination before any real-run claim. A source feature at54dcefbc is not proof of its deployment. Dropping the local room removes draft1's local storage/destination dependency and its lost-reply witness. M1's install route remains optional and held if deployment is needed.\n\nF1 high, partly resolved — S1 now explicitly sets roles' actions and S3 names issue.approve only for people, which resolves that part of the previous grant gap. The Change walkthrough still says the other agent reviews after both agents contributed. A default agent lacks change.review (membership.ts:144-165); a contributing author is additionally refused author-cannot-review (change.ts:927-929), regardless of grant. Specify the one counted approval, including ownerMayReview/controller policy if the single owner supplies it (reservation.ts:237-246). Agent feedback can remain feedback. Witness a complete native merge with that actual approval and real rules/membership, not a scripted approving grant. On an existing shared room, the runbook must preserve current role lists when adding actions: set-actions replaces the entire list, as the cited guide states.\n\nF2 high, unresolved — The walkthrough revises intent conditions after accepting commitments, but its commitments/reports still have fixed old conditionsAt/termsAt (issue.ts:63-78,350-360,551-575). It also no longer describes accepting both agents' reports before selecting them. State the exact adoption/cancellation/new-offer or explicitly accepted old-input path and restore the missing native report-acceptance step. Show current intent criteria, commitment terms and report terms separately. The new question approval's optional criteriaAt and decide's listed guards do not by themselves prove adoption of current criteria; either bind that claim to the exact criteria version, or clearly say the approval approves only the question text and rely on the owner's separately recorded revise for criteria. Witness resumption under the chosen agreement and no relabelling of old-terms work.\n\nF3 high, unresolved — S7 still puts execution of candidate node tests and checker signing in one local script without an execution trust boundary. Moving the room off the desktop does not stop candidate tests reading the local signing key or configuration. State a concrete local runner boundary that excludes signer/room credentials and outside writes, with bounded execution and job/tree/configuration-bound results through the reviewed signing path (runner.ts:32-40; sandbox.ts:7-33; signing.ts:10-24). The smaller alternative remains an explicitly trusted, separately reviewed fixed-fixture-only experiment, with no arbitrary candidate execution or isolation claim. Choose one and witness it; no deployment prerequisite is requested.\n\nF4 medium, unresolved — S0 tests reachability/rendering but needs an acceptance condition for WHO may reach the fixed owner signer (mcp.ts:77-102), especially now it points at a real hosted room. Use a dedicated test configuration, record allowed caller contexts and require denial outside them before routing owner-capable tools through a tunnel. A workspace association, tunnel identifier, first write prompt or lack of inbound public port is not proof of individual exclusivity. Preserve loopback bearer and Origin checks; use the throwaway write tool to probe safely. If suitable authorization cannot be established, use the already-proposed Claude stdio fallback. Correct H1's unchanged assertion that both hosts universally require OAuth: current official Claude remote auth supports none and limited static headers; OpenAI custom MCP supports no auth. OAuth remains the proposed authenticated multi-user route. Primary docs checked16Oct: https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/secure-mcp-tunnels ; https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/custom-mcp-server ; https://claude.com/docs/connectors/building/authentication .\n\nF5 medium, unresolved — Killing a blocked session does not arrange a handover. Only the current performer can offer it, and a successor cannot accept while the hold is live (issue.ts:447-467). Specify same-member/key restart, a handover offered before the kill, or another separately authorized sequence. Include the hold-ending step/time and original block/decision references. Same-identity fresh-session resumption is the smaller valid test; do not call it proof of a new-member takeover.\n\nF6 medium, partly simplified — Moving BRIEF.md into the package removes the need for a general Git file-read feature just to retrieve it. Still state how the brief's exact pinned bytes and evidence reach the fresh conversation, and where the substantive Decision view renders the approved text/context and performs version-bound actions. S2's view kit plus S6's diff-only read does not state that path; an unchanged brief is not a diff. A bounded package resource/projection can suffice. Label semantic conflict recognition as the owner's/model's comparison unless actually implementing a native semantic check. Under the one-host fallback, explicitly leave the two-host pass item pending instead of S9 claiming all six passed.\n\nArchitecture conclusion: hosted-room/data/local separation and the smaller question-approval model supported, subject to S0 and these unresolved native-flow dependencies. Security conclusion: changes still required on S7 trust and S0 access to owner signing authority. Simplification conclusion: preserve the new scope and avoid restoring the removed local-room work; the existing-authority/terms/same-key restart alternatives and a small pinned context resource are sufficient directions. S3's version-bound requests/approvals are a useful reuse of the native pattern; this review is not implementation approval or a commission for broader membership/platform changes.\n\nValidation: complete draft2 read and its new source references checked at the exact head; one added Markdown file against54dcefbc, relative proposal link valid, diff --check clean. Runtime/source/test bytes are unchanged. The primary host/standard/version evidence checked during draft1 remains applicable; no account probe or deployed-room inspection was run. No gate repetition for a prose-only candidate, source edit, private credential access, provider operation, push or deployment.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:602fe14a3700aaf16b8aed58a176205eacebe677","binding":"assigned","head":"88fc23a931894925cad8d445c5707b267b461a33","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5071b9a15ff0d65933cde147f492970fa3386d3f\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:437379213232e582a8121ba398e1eea6f9ee5385\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5071b9a15ff0d65933cde147f492970fa3386d3f","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}